     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I have two really large data frames:<div><br></div><div>df1- 150mb, 1 million obs of 13 vars</div><div><br></div><div>df2- 210mb, 1.2 million obs of 23 vars</div><div><br></div><div>i&#39;m attempting the following:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;dplyr&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>new_df </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> left_join</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">df1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> df2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#008\">by</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;one_common_var&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></div></code></div><br></div><div><br></div><div>this process cranks away for about 5mins, and then fails, with a cherry bomb crash in rstudio, and with the memory addressed by r getting up to ~70GB right before the crash.</div><div><br></div><div>is there a way to do this?</div><div><br></div><div>thanks for any advice.</div><div><br></div><div>here are my system specs:</div><div><br></div><div>Macbook Pro</div><div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<p>2.3 GHz Intel Core i7</p><p>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p>16 GB 1600 MHz DDR3</p><p>500GB solid state HD, w/ 300GB free/available</p><p>rstudio v 0.99.441</p><p>dplyr v 0.4.1.9000</p><p>readxl v 0.1.0.9000 (used to load df1)</p><p>readr v 0.1.0 (used to load df2)</p></div></div>"
